---
TDL: 0.2
Shell: 0.1
Name: Menu
---

# The content of a Popup that is a menu (Standard Modules > Menu and MenuItem): a column of
# MenuItems with the role MENU. The Popup is the surface (its `Attach`, `Gap`, `Style`...); the Menu
# takes the Popup's width from its items (at least 160 pixels).
#   Popup File_Menu { Style { Background: $color.surface_raised, Corner_Radius: 8 }
#       Children { Menu { MenuItem { Text: "New", On_Click: ... } MenuItem { Separator: true } } } }
# A Button opens it with `On_Click { Action: Show, Target: File_Menu, Data { Id: 7 } }`; the items
# read `caller.data`. A click on an item runs its action and closes the menu.
# Keys: a Menu opened from the keyboard takes the focus (one Tab stop). Up and Down move the lit
# row (round the ends, over a disabled row), Home and End go to the first and the last, Enter and
# Space run it (a row with a submenu opens it), Right opens the submenu of the lit row, Left closes
# a submenu, and Escape closes the innermost level; Escape on the first menu closes it and gives the
# focus back to the block it was opened from. The pointer on a row takes the light from the keys.
Module {
    Params {
        Label { Type: string, Default: "" }
    }
    FlexBox {
        Name: Root
        Role: MENU
        Label: <| params.Label |>
        Flex: VERTICAL
        Min_Width: 160
        Padding: <| space.step_2 |>
        Children { Content { } }
    }
}
